package CanvasNet {
    part def MermaidScenePositions {
        doc /* The internal static ScenePositions of the Mermaid Scenegraph subsystem (stateless and thread-safe): the positions of the features of a laid-out scene, from the ScenePositionTag records (kind, id, text, source line, ends, value, explicit aim, and whether the pixel aims along the path) that the renderers set on the SceneItem.Position of the items they draw, in the pixels of the surface a placement draws on. Report does nothing when the render options have no PositionHandler and otherwise delivers what Collect returns; MermaidDocument calls it in both Render overloads with the placement before painting. Collect walks the scene with the accumulated group translations, skips a kind the PositionKindFilter rejects before computing any geometry, and merges the items whose tags have the same kind and id into one feature (a self-loop drawn in three pieces, a gantt section drawn as one band per row, a commit bullet drawn as several shapes) whose box is the union of their geometry bounds (Scene.BoundsOf: curves exactly, stroke not included, group translations applied). The pixel is the explicit aim of the tag when it has one (a pie slice at its mid-angle and mid-radius, a commit at its point), else, for a tag that aims along its path (edges and messages), the arc-length midpoint of the joined paths (PathMidpoint: lines, curves, and arcs flattened), else the center of the box. The features are ordered by kind in KindOrder (title, group, node, participant, task, milestone, section, slice, block, commit, branch, tag, edge, message, note), then by source line (a feature without a line last), then by drawing order; an edge or message gets its 0-based Index among the features of its kind with the same ends; the text is trimmed; and the box and the pixel are mapped from scene units to the surface by the scale and offset of the placement. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid/Scenegraph/ScenePositions.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid.Tests/Scenegraph/ScenePositionsTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Mermaid.Tests/MermaidDocumentPositionTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-mermaid/scenegraph/scene-positions.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-mermaid/scenegraph/scene-positions.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-mermaid/scenegraph/scene-positions.yaml */
    }
}
